20age","name":"archived due to age","color":"eeeeee","default":false,"description":"This issue has been archived; please open a new issue for any further discussion"}],"state":"closed","locked":true,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":13,"created_at":"2014-06-05T20:08:50Z","updated_at":"2018-02-07T02:03:59Z","closed_at":"2015-02-07T21:13:19Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I wanted to isolate this generic problem further before opening this up but I've been at it for about two days now and I just wanted to see if anyone else has seen this or has any ideas. With the latest version of eslint there seems to be a significant memory leak, enough to cause Node to run out of memory:\n\n```\nFATAL ERROR: CALL_AND_RETRY_2 Allocation failed - process out of memory\n```\n\nThis happens when running eslint on Windows on a directory of 4,463 items totaling 118.6mb. The process memory approached 1.5gb shortly before this error. When run on the same directory on OS X the memory also seems to increase but not enough to be fatal.\n\nI'm trying to profile it and narrow down the naughty code, but Node's memory profiling tools seem to be a little lacking. I'm fumbling around with memwatch heap diffs at the moment, but they're not granular enough to do much narrowing down.\n","closed_by":{"login":"nzakas","id":38546,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NTQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38546?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas","html_url":"https://github.com/nzakas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nzakas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/use